+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Myrtle Beach the fastest growing city in America?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The Myrtle Beach metro area, which is all of Horry County, grew the second fastest in the country from mid-2024 to mid-2025, behind Ocala, Florida. The City of Myrtle Beach itself has about 41,000 people, and most of the growth is outside city limits."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are people leaving Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, about 9,100 households a year, while about 15,000 move in. The top places they go are Georgetown and Charleston counties in South Carolina and Brunswick County, North Carolina."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where do most people moving to Myrtle Beach come from?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Outside South Carolina, the most households come from Suffolk County on Long Island, then Brunswick, Mecklenburg and Wake counties in North Carolina. About six in ten Horry County residents were born in another state."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is it cheaper to live in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Homes and property tax usually cost less than where most movers come from. A typical home in Horry County is valued at about $320,000, and an owner who lives in the home typically pays about $944 a year in property tax. Pay is lower too."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does South Carolina tax Social Security?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. South Carolina does not tax Social Security, and military retirement pay is not taxed either."}}]}</script>
